#: src/languages/elixir.md:131
msgid "Using the Tailwind CSS Language Server with HEEx"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:133
msgid ""
"To get all features (autocomplete, linting, and hover docs) from the "
"[Tailwind CSS language server](https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss-"
"intellisense/tree/HEAD/packages/tailwindcss-language-server#readme) in HEEx "
"files, add the following to your settings file ([how to edit](../configuring-"
"zed.md#settings-files)):"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:138
msgid "\"tailwindcss-language-server\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:140
msgid "\"includeLanguages\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:141
msgid "\"phoenix-heex\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:141
msgid "\"html\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:143
msgid "\"experimental\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:144
msgid "\"classRegex\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:144
msgid "\"class=\\\"([^\\\"]*)\\\"\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:144
msgid "\"class='([^']*)'\""
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:152
msgid ""
"With these settings, you will get completions for Tailwind CSS classes in "
"HEEx template files. Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/elixir.md:154
msgid ""
"```heex\n"
"<%!-- Standard class attribute --%>\n"
"<div class=\"flex items-center <completion here>\">\n"
"  <p class=\"text-lg font-bold <completion here>\">Hello World</p>\n"
"</div>\n"
"\n"
"<%!-- With Elixir expression --%>\n"
"<div class={\"flex #{@custom_class} <completion here>\"}>\n"
"  Content\n"
"</div>\n"
"\n"
"<%!-- With Phoenix function --%>\n"
"<div class={class_list([\"flex\", \"items-center\", \"<completion here>\"])}"
">\n"
"  Content\n"
"</div>\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
